mlflow:auth:ExperimentPermission.description:
Grants a user a permission level on an MLflow experiment. Valid `permission` values are `READ`, `EDIT`, `MANAGE` and `NO_PERMISSIONS`; only `permission` can be updated in place (changing the experiment or user replaces the grant).

> **Requires the MLflow auth app.** These resources call the [MLflow authentication REST API](https://mlflow.org/docs/latest/auth/rest-api.html), which is only available when the tracking server runs with the `mlflow.server.auth` app enabled (e.g. `mlflow server --app-name basic-auth`).

{{% examples %}}
## Example Usage

{{% example %}}
{{< chooser language "typescript,python,go" >}}
{{% choosable language typescript %}}
```typescript
import * as mlflow from "@baubap/mlflow";

const readAccess = new mlflow.auth.ExperimentPermission("read-access", {
    experimentId: "0",
    username: "jdoe",
    permission: "READ",
});
```
{{% /choosable %}}
{{% choosable language python %}}
```python
import baubap_mlflow as mlflow

read_access = mlflow.auth.ExperimentPermission("read-access",
    experiment_id="0",
    username="jdoe",
    permission="READ")
```
{{% /choosable %}}
{{% choosable language go %}}
```go
_, err := auth.NewExperimentPermission(ctx, "read-access", &auth.ExperimentPermissionArgs{
    ExperimentId: pulumi.String("0"),
    Username:     pulumi.String("jdoe"),
    Permission:   pulumi.String("READ"),
})
```
{{% /choosable %}}
{{< /chooser >}}
{{% /example %}}
{{% /examples %}}

## Import

Import an existing resource with its id:

```sh
$ pulumi import mlflow:auth:ExperimentPermission example <experimentId>/<username>
```

